# CVE-2026-48068: Fix server crash when handling invalid requests
#
# A malformed HTTP/2 stream initiation triggers an uncaught error event in
# the server, crashing the process. Move the `error` handler from the
# BaseServerInterceptingCall constructor (which is created lazily, after
# stream errors may already have fired) up to the Server stream entry
# points (_channelzHandler and _streamHandler), so the handler is attached
# the moment the stream is observed.
#
# Origin: internal-reuse from sibling @grpc/grpc-js 1.13.2 patch
#         (upstream commit 455efce8acb7fb249652a74c1618a6d7daf1faba in
#         https://github.com/grpc/grpc-node, released in 1.12.7)
# Adapted-To: @grpc/grpc-js 1.12.2 (npm) - context lines re-anchored
#             with function-name disambiguation; the two server.ts hunks
#             share identical anchor text and required tighter context.
